::Fundamentals: Tokens, temperature, max tokens, top-p, frequency & presence penalties::

Tokens:

What it is: The smallest unit of text the AI understands. Not exactly a word — could be a word, part of a word, or punctuation.

Example:

Sentence: “I love AI.”

Tokens: ["I", " love", " AI", "."] → 4 tokens.

Why it matters: Pricing, memory, and response length all depend on number of tokens.

 2. Temperature

Controls creativity vs. accuracy.

Scale: 0 → 1+ (sometimes up to 2).

Low (0–0.3): More predictable, factual, repeatable. (Good for coding, finance, instructions).

Medium (0.5–0.7): Balanced creativity + accuracy.

High (0.8–1.0+): More random, imaginative. (Good for brainstorming, poetry, creative writing).

 3. Max Tokens

The cap on response length.

If you set max_tokens=100, the AI won’t generate more than ~100 tokens in the reply.

Useful to:

Prevent overly long answers.

Control costs.

 4. Top-p (a.k.a. Nucleus Sampling)

Another way to control randomness.

Instead of temperature, it looks at probability distribution of words and only keeps the top % of most likely words.

top-p=0.9: Only consider words that together make up 90% probability.

 Often used with or instead of temperature.

 5. Frequency Penalty

Discourages repetition of the same words/sentences.

Example: Without penalty → “AI is great, AI is great, AI is great.”

With higher penalty → AI avoids repeating and tries new phrasing.

 6. Presence Penalty

Encourages introducing new topics.

Low value → AI may stick to the same theme.

High value → AI explores broader topics (useful in brainstorming).

 Summary:

Imagine asking: “Write a poem about cloud computing.”

Temperature=0.2, top-p=0.9: Simple, factual, less poetic.

Temperature=0.9, top-p=0.95: Creative, unpredictable, funny metaphors.

High frequency penalty: Won’t repeat “cloud” 10 times.

High presence penalty: Might bring in new ideas like “rainbows,” “servers,” “lightning.”

In shorter way :

Tokens = building blocks of language.

Temperature & Top-p = randomness vs. focus.

Max tokens = response length limit.

Frequency & Presence penalties = control repetition and topic variety.
